sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 remediation-round evaluation of `1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py` (87.1/100, down from 90.7 in Pass 2 although the model is substantially more faithful). Both v2 remediation items were closed: the kinematic 2D template that v2 had credited as a solver is replaced by a genuine 2D coupled cell-ECM PDE on a limb paddle with a moving free-boundary AER front (`_simulate_2d_aer_free_boundary_outgrowth`, L427-628) that produces the forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] hierarchies from a seeded proximal nucleus plus noise, lays them down in proximo-distal order (onset 30.0 < 56.5 < 78.5) and reproduces the Saunders (1948) AER-ablation truncation series [1, 1, 2, 3]; and the mechanics are hybridised with Raspopovic (2014) Bmp-Sox9-Wnt kinetics (`hybrid_mechanochemical_bsw_jacobian`, L717-759; `simulate_1d_hybrid_mechanochemical_bsw`, L816-902) showing a synergy window (tau_c 1.44 -> 0.35) and a 2x2 factorial [0, 0, 0, 4] at tau = 0.85 with corr(S, B) = -0.988. The same work exposed that the solvers' drift kernel is 12.7% off the analytic threshold, that the 1D wavelength validation is tautological, that the reference JSON's canonical parameters were never the script's, and that in 2D the autopod count is partly inherited by bifurcation rather than set by W / lambda_c; these drive the lower, more honest scores. 9 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (6 new, 0 sorrys) and 14 reference-anchored measurements (9 new). Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 86.1, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py at d58a084, image/png, 975928 B, 2604×2268 px, artifact_sha256 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff (sha256 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff), spec_fingerprint 176fd41f0d953b7b1e5e1437961112bdacb6e1e1e0faf2536dab887008a3d35d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 176fd41f0d953b7b1e5e1437961112bdacb6e1e1e0faf2536dab887008a3d35d; artifact_sha256: 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json=f2c0be56cbef12c2..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg=8030c8291c3a6d5b..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/scout_manifest.json=cb9d73c33c4113e4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system; the AER maintains a distal recruitment/progress zone and condensations are laid down proximo-distally | Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod) and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders) | Saunders (1948): removing the chick-wing AER at progressively later stages leaves progressively more distal skeletal parts (proximo-distal sequence of origin) | Raspopovic et al. (2014): a Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing network with Sox9 out of phase with Bmp and Wnt patterns the digits; reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with analytic tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9597 (lambda_c = 6.5472) and the 1D spectral-pseudospectral cell-ECM solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] on periodic domains W = m lambda_c with seeded m-cosine perturbations | A 2D coupled cell-ECM PDE on a limb paddle with a moving free-boundary AER front (progress-zone traction suppression and proliferation, AER regression, anisotropic PD cell diffusion a_y = 3, ectoderm-balanced prestress) producing the forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] hierarchies from a seeded proximal nucleus plus noise, with proximo-distal onset order and the Saunders (1948) ablation series [1, 1, 2, 3] | A 4x4 hybrid Jacobian and 1D hybrid PDE coupling the mechanics to Raspopovic (2014) BSW kinetics (tau(1 + alpha_S S), +kappa_S (n - N_0)), with wavelength-matched ligand diffusivities, showing tau_c lowering 1.44 -> 0.35 and a 2x2 factorial [0, 0, 0, 4] at tau = 0.85 | Morphological segmentation of the vendored Oedipina ecuatoriana specimen giving [1, 2, 4] / [1, 2, 5] hierarchies, autopod spacings 39.0 / 41.25 px and the zeugopod/autopod spacing ratio compared with the 2D PDE (1.235 vs 1.373); transfer_boundary: The 2D domain is a Fourier-periodic box with a diffuse (tanh) competence field, not a sharp Neumann boundary; the ECM force balance is reduced to a component-wise Helmholtz operator (no shear/Poisson coupling, no ECM density equation) and the viscous relaxation rate 1/(mu + 0.15) is ad hoc | The solvers' drift kernel includes mu k^2 in the quasi-static stiffness, so their effective tau_c (1.4397) is 12.7% above the analytic 1.2776 shown in Panels A/D; all supercritical regimes used exceed both | Only the proximal humeral/femoral nucleus is seeded in the 2D solver; the stylopod width W = 1.4 lambda_c is a tuned choice (W = 1.0 is marginal), and the autopod count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation rather than set by W / lambda_c | The BSW parameters are copied from the Slot 016 reference JSON, rescaled in diffusivity to match lambda_c; the Saunders (1948) comparison is a qualitative stage-to-segment mapping, not digitised data; lengths are in lambda_c units with no micron calibration against the specimen; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element limb, explicit ECM density/advection, joint/phalangeal segmentation of the rods, Hoxd13 gene-dosage polydactyly scaling (Slot 017), or quantitative reproduction of the full Raspopovic (2014) 2D autopod (Slot 016)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:312-313 and :1129-1137 — measurement 2 (1D autopod wavelength = lambda_c, CV = 0.0000) is exact by construction because the periodic domain is W = 4 lambda_c and the m = 4 cosine is seeded. Replace it with a noise-only 1D run on a long domain (W >= 12 lambda_c) and report the emergent dominant wavelength and its error against lambda_c.",
            "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:329 and :508 — the drift kernel i k sigma_hat / (E k^2 + s + mu k^2) places the viscous term in the quasi-static stiffness, so the 1D and 2D solvers' effective threshold is tau_c = 1.4397 while Panels A/D, measurement 1 and the Lean law report the analytic 1.2776 (measurement 14, L1251-1261). Either solve the Kelvin-Voigt balance properly (mu k^2 du/dt + (E k^2 + s) u = i k sigma_hat and advect cells with du/dt) or re-derive and display the solver's own marginal curve.",
            "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:444-446 and :517-523 — the 2D autopod count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation of the zeugopod rods (W_autopod = 3.0 ... 4.5 lambda_c all gave 4 rods during tuning) and the stylopod only condenses for W_stylopod in roughly [1.3, 1.5] lambda_c, so the 2D dynamics does not follow the m = round(W / lambda_c) staircase that Panel D draws. Add a shipped W_autopod sweep (3.0 ... 6.0) and a W_stylopod sweep as measurements, and overlay the 2D staircase on Panel D.",
            "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:566 and :579 — the ectoderm-balanced prestress sigma_drive = chi (1 - g_pz) [sigma_cell(n) - sigma_cell(N_0)] and the progress-zone mitotic noise are modelling choices that remove a boundary-rim artefact; add an ablation (bare penalised mask, no noise) as a measurement so the dependence of the 1 -> 2 -> 4 result on these choices is quantified rather than argued in the docstring.",
            "remediation needed: 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py:674-686 — BSW_PARAMS are copied from datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_reference.json rather than read from it with its SHA-256; read the Slot 016 fixture at runtime (verify its digest) so the hybrid inherits its provenance, and add a micron/hour calibration of lambda_c and v_AER against the specimen scale and chick outgrowth rates.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json:102-115 vs :116-137 — `canonical_parameters` (D_1 = 0.08, D_2 = 0.0025, s = 0.5, r = 0.2, tau_stylopod = 1.48) were never the script's values; the new `script_default_parameters` block discloses this. Reconcile: either adopt the vendored values in the script (re-deriving tau_c, lambda_c) or trace each script default to a source and retire the stale block; then SHA-256-pin the reference JSON." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.871"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

